 "_doc": "luceneutil arms of branch g-luceneutil (GENERIC-PLAN section 5). Values in {braces} are params: the IO sizes come from the IO configuration (8 KiB block, 32 KiB random, 128 KiB sequential); the K2 / ORPF / TOPK values and the CORE set must be copied from artifacts-final.json and the final POC report before phase B (recorded per arm in session.json). Switch names are checked against switches.json (generated from the fork). Stock Lucene arms carry no switches. The index variants are built by luceneutil (run_luceneutil.py index) on EBS and copied with checksums to EFS (run_luceneutil.py copy). Index builds use luceneutil's own defaults (1 indexing thread, LogDocMergePolicy, SerialMergeScheduler): the build is deterministic, so every variant (stock, POC-built stock codec, split BKD, DualNav) has the same doc ids and the same segments, and only the codec differs between variants. Arm labels ARM:STORAGE@REPEAT interleave one arm on EBS and EFS in one session.",
